        {
          "title": "Generics Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Generic Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "A generic is a ==type-level parameter==: `function id<T>(x: T): T`",
                "One declaration works for **many types** without losing type info"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "any",
                "T"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Input type",
                  "{red:discarded}",
                  "{green:linked to output}"
                ],
                [
                  "`id(5)` returns",
                  "`any`",
                  "literal `5`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Inference and Erasure",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Inferred from call arguments: `id('a')` gives T = `'a'`",
                "Pass explicitly when inference fails: `id<string>('a')`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "function id<T>(x: T): T { return x }",
                "id(5)           // T = 5",
                "id('a')         // T = 'a'",
                "id<string>('a') // T = string"
              ],
              "note": "explicit argument overrides inference"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Erased at runtime",
              "text": "T exists only for the compiler. So no `new T()` and no `typeof T`."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**What do generics fix over `any`?** T links input to output, so type info survives",
                "**Available at runtime?** No, erased; `new T()` is impossible",
                "**Infer or explicit?** Inferred from arguments; explicit when no argument fixes T"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Generic Functions, Interfaces and Classes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Generic Functions, Interfaces and Classes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Declaring Generics",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Form",
                "Declare",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Function",
                  "`function first<T>(a: T[]): T | undefined { return a[0]; }`",
                  "`first([1, 2])`"
                ],
                [
                  "Interface",
                  "`interface Box<T> { value: T }`",
                  "`Box<number>`"
                ],
                [
                  "Call signature",
                  "`interface Fn<T> { (x: T): T }`",
                  "`Fn<string>`"
                ],
                [
                  "Alias",
                  "`type Pair<A, B> = [A, B]`",
                  "`Pair<string, number>`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Generic Class",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`new Stack<number>()` fixes ==T== for that instance"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "class Stack<T> {",
                "  private items: T[] = [];",
                "  push(x: T) { this.items.push(x) }",
                "  pop(): T | undefined { return this.items.pop() }",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Rules",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Arrow in `.tsx`: write `<T,>(x: T) => x`; the comma stops JSX parsing",
                "Several params are ==comma-separated==; supply each unless defaulted"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Static",
              "text": "Static members cannot use `T`: it belongs to the ==instance side== only."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Declare a generic class?** `class C<T> {}`, then `new C<number>()`",
                "**Static using T?** Statics live on the constructor, not on instances, so no `T`",
                "**Interface vs alias?** Interface extends and merges; alias also names unions and tuples"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Constraints with extends",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Constraints with extends",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Constraint syntax",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`T extends { length: number }`: callers may pass only types that have ==length==",
                "Bare `T` is unknown-like, so `x.length` {red:errors}",
                "`T` keeps the specific type: `len([1, 2])` gives `T = number[]`, `len('abc')` gives `T = string`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "function len<T extends { length: number }>(x: T) {",
                "  return x.length",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "accepts string, array, any object with length"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Dependent params and constructors",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`K extends keyof T` ties the ==key== to the object",
                "`T extends new (...a: any[]) => object` accepts a ==class== you can `new`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "function pick<T, K extends keyof T>(o: T, k: K): T[K]",
                "function make<T extends new (...a: any[]) => object>(C: T) {",
                "  return new C()",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**extends in a constraint?** It means ==assignable to==, not class inheritance",
                "**Why no `.length` on bare T?** T could be anything, so only `unknown` members exist",
                "**One param depending on another?** `K extends keyof T`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Floor, not replacement",
              "text": "The constraint only ==checks== the argument. `T` is still inferred from it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Defaults, keyof and Indexed Access",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Defaults, keyof and Indexed Access",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Default type parameters",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`interface Res<T = unknown> { data: T }`, so `Res` means `Res<unknown>`",
                "Applied only when T is ==not given== and ==not inferred==",
                "Defaulted params go ==after== required ones",
                "Default must satisfy the constraint: `<T extends object = {}>`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. keyof and indexed access",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Gives"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`keyof {a: 1; b: 2}`",
                  "`'a' | 'b'`"
                ],
                [
                  "`keyof any[]`",
                  "`number` + method names"
                ],
                [
                  "`keyof {[k: string]: X}`",
                  "`string | number`"
                ],
                [
                  "`User['id']`",
                  "type of property `id`"
                ],
                [
                  "`T[number]`",
                  "array element type"
                ],
                [
                  "`T[keyof T]`",
                  "union of all value types"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Typed getter",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`K extends keyof T`: wrong keys fail at ==compile time==",
                "`T[K]` makes the return type ==exact==, not a union"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "function get<T, K extends keyof T>(o: T, k: K): T[K] { return o[k] }",
                "get({ id: 1 }, 'id')  // number",
                "get({ id: 1 }, 'x')   // error"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview point",
              "items": [
                "**keyof**: key union; arrays add `number`, index signatures `string | number`",
                "**T[K]**: looks up K's own type",
                "**Default**: only if T is not given or inferred"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common Generic Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common Generic Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Smells in the signature",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`function f<T>(x: T): void`: ==T used once== relates nothing, so it is a smell",
                "Each T should link ==two positions==, such as param and return",
                "`as T` or `{} as T` ==hides errors==; the compiler cannot verify it"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Constraint traps",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mistake",
                "Why it fails",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`T extends string`, `return 'a'`",
                  "T may be a narrower literal",
                  "Return `string`"
                ],
                [
                  "`typeof x === 'string'`",
                  "Does not narrow `T` itself",
                  "Overloads or conditional types"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Untyped keys",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Key typed `string`: implicit any on `o[k]`, safety lost",
                "Use ==K extends keyof T== instead"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "typescript",
              "lines": [
                "function get<T, K extends keyof T>(",
                "  o: T, k: K",
                "): T[K] {",
                "  return o[k];",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "The caller picks T, so you cannot return a concrete value for it. To debug inference, hover the call or pass `<T>` explicitly."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
